# AI-Researcher — always-on context

A local-first research engine for quantum computing and AI literature, single user.
Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root — it is the shared source of truth across Codex, Cursor,
and Claude Code, and it governs everything below.

## Work comes from task files, not chat

```
docs/superpowers/projects/ai-researcher-app/
  PROJECT.md                 # cross-phase architecture
  phase-N/PHASE.md           # phase scope, requirements, acceptance
  phase-N/NN-task-name.md    # one task = one PR
```

Before starting: read the task file → its `PHASE.md` → `PROJECT.md`. A task is done only
when every acceptance criterion passes by running its stated command.

Tasks form a strict chain via `depends_on_task` frontmatter. Do not start a task whose
predecessor has not merged.

## Cursor owns phase 4

- Phase 4 — Monitoring, Discourse & Temporal Digests

Codex owns phases 1–3 (moved from Cursor once Codex tokens were available). These run
manually — no autonomous loop moves board cards.
Board: https://github.com/users/BankNatchapol/projects/6

## Stack

Python 3.11+ · `uv` (not Poetry, not pip) · `pytest` · `ruff` (not black/flake8) ·
PostgreSQL plain · GROBID in Docker · CLI model gateway (claude -p / codex exec, no API
keys) · CLI + MCP over one core library.

```bash
uv run pytest && uv run ruff check .
```

Both must pass before any PR.
